{
  "total": 238,
  "totalPage": 5,
  "page": 5,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdf2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3082,
      "bookHadithIndex": 201,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir that the Prophet (ﷺ) was treated with cupping when he was in the state of Ihram, because he did not feel well",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3082-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3082-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3082-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3082-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdf3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3083,
      "bookHadithIndex": 202,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to put oil on his head when he was in the state of Ihram, but not oil that was perfumed",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3083-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3083-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3083-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdf4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3084,
      "bookHadithIndex": 203,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas that a man’s neck was broken by his mount (from falling) while he was in the state of Ihram. The Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Wash him with water and lote leaves, and shroud him in his two garments, but do not cover his face or his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah.” Another chain reports the same except a different verb was used for the break of the neck and he said \"do not bring him near perfume, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3084-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3084-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3084-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3084-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdf5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3085,
      "bookHadithIndex": 204,
      "text": "It was narrated that Jabir said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stipulated (the penalty of) a man for a hyena killed by a man in Ihram, and he considered it as game.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3085-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3085-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3085-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3085-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdf6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3086,
      "bookHadithIndex": 205,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, concerning an ostrich egg taken by a Muhrim:“Its cost (must be paid as a penalty).”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3086-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3086-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3086-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3086-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdf7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3087,
      "bookHadithIndex": 206,
      "text": "It was narrated from ‘Aishah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“There are five vermin that might be killed whether one is in or outside the sacred precincts: the snake, the speckled crow, the mouse, the vicious dog, and the kite.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3087-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3087-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3087-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3087-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdf8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3088,
      "bookHadithIndex": 207,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“There are five animals, for which there is no sin on a person if he kills them” – or he said: “if he kills them when in Ihram – the scorpion, the crow, the kite, the mouse and the vicious dog.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3088-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3088-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3088-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3088-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdf9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3089,
      "bookHadithIndex": 208,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Sa’eed that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:‘The one in Ihram may kill the snake, the scorpion, the aggressive predator, the vicious dog and the harmful mouse.” It was said to him: “Why is it said that they are harmful?” He said:* “Because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) woke up because of one, and it had taken the wick (of the lamp) to burn down the house.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3089-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3089-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3089-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3089-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdfa",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3090,
      "bookHadithIndex": 209,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn ‘Abbas said:“Sa;b bin Jaththamah told us: ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by me when I was in Abwa’ or Waddan, and I gave him some meat of a wild donkey, but he gave it back to me, and when he saw from my face that I was upset, he said: ‘The only reason that we are giving it back is that we are in Ihram.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3090-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3090-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3090-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3090-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdfb",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3091,
      "bookHadithIndex": 210,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Ali bin Abu Talib said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) brought some meat from some game when he was in Ihram, and he did not eat it.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3091-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3091-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3091-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3091-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdfc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3092,
      "bookHadithIndex": 211,
      "text": "It was narrated from Talhah bin ‘Ubaidullah that the Prophet (ﷺ) gave him some wild donkey meat, and told him to distribute it among his Companions, who were in Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3092-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Isnaad Malool"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3092-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Isnaad Malool"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3092-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdfd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3093,
      "bookHadithIndex": 212,
      "text": "It was narrated from ‘Abdullah bin Abu Qatadah that his father said:“I went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at the time of Hudaibiyah, and his Companions entered Ihram, but I did not. I saw a donkey do I hunted it. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and told him: ‘I had not entered Ihram, and I was hunting it for you.’ The Prophet (ﷺ) told his Companions to eat it, but he did not eat from it, because I told him that I had hunted it for him.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3093-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3093-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3093-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3093-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdfe",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3094,
      "bookHadithIndex": 213,
      "text": "‘Aishah the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) said; “The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to send the sacrificial animal from Al-Madinah, and I would twist the garlands for his sacrificial animal, then, he would not (because of that) avoid the things that the one in Ihram avoids.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3094-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3094-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3094-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3094-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cdff",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3095,
      "bookHadithIndex": 214,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Aishah the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“I used to twist the garlands for the sacrificial animal of the Prophet (ﷺ), and his sacrificial animal would be garlanded and sent (to Makkah), and he would stay (in Al-Madinah) without avoiding any of the things that the one in Ihram avoids.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3095-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3095-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3095-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3095-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce00",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3096,
      "bookHadithIndex": 215,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“On one occasion the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent sheep to the House, and he garlanded them.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3096-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3096-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3096-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3096-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce01",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3097,
      "bookHadithIndex": 216,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas that the Prophet (ﷺ) marked the sacrificial animal on the right side of the hump and wiped away the blood",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3097-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3097-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3097-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3097-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce02",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3098,
      "bookHadithIndex": 217,
      "text": "It was narrated from ‘Aishah that the Prophet (ﷺ) garlanded, and marked, and sent (the sacrificial animals), but he did not avoid anything that the one in Ihram avoids",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3098-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3098-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3098-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3098-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce03",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3099,
      "bookHadithIndex": 218,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Ali bin Abu Talib said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded me to look after his sacrificial camels, to share out their covers and skins, and not to give the butcher any of it. He said: ‘We will give him (his wages).’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3099-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3099-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3099-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3099-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce04",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3100,
      "bookHadithIndex": 219,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas that among the sacrificial animals the Prophet (ﷺ) included a (male) camel belonging to Abu Jahl, which had a silver nose ring",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3100-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3100-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3100-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce05",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3101,
      "bookHadithIndex": 220,
      "text": "It was narrated from Iyas bin Salamah, from his father, that the Prophet (ﷺ) had a (male) camel among his sacrificial animals",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3101-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3101-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3101-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce06",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3102,
      "bookHadithIndex": 221,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that the Prophet (ﷺ) bought his sacrificial animal from Qudaid",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3102-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3102-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3102-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce07",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3103,
      "bookHadithIndex": 222,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw a man driving a camel and said:“Ride it.” He said: “It is a sacrificial animal.” He said: “Ride it, woe to you!”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3103-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3103-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3103-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3103-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce08",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3104,
      "bookHadithIndex": 223,
      "text": "It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Prophet (ﷺ) was brought a sacrificial animal and he said (to the man driving the animal):“Ride it.” He said: “It is a sacrificial animal.” He said: “Ride it.” He said: “I saw him riding it with the Prophet (ﷺ), and there was a sandal (tied) around its neck.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3104-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3104-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3104-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3104-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce09",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3105,
      "bookHadithIndex": 224,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas that Dhu’aib Al-Khuza’i narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to send the sacrificial animals with him, then he would say:“If any of them becomes unfit and you are afraid that it will die, then slaughter it, dip the sandal (tied around its neck) in its blood and place it on its side, but neither you nor any of your companions should eat anything from it.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3105-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3105-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3105-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3105-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce0a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3106,
      "bookHadithIndex": 225,
      "text": "It was narrated that Najiyah Al-Khuza’i – in his narration, ‘Amr (one of the narrators) said that he was the one who looked after the sacrificial animals of the Prophet (ﷺ) – said:“I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what should I do with those sacrificial animals that become unfit?’ He said: ‘Slaughter them, dip its sandal in its blood, then place it on its side, and leave them for the people to eat.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3106-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3106-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3106-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3106-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce0b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3107,
      "bookHadithIndex": 226,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Alqamah bin Nadlah said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), Abu Bakr and ‘Umar died, and the houses in Makkah were still called free. Whoever needed to, lived there, and whoever had no need of them allowed others to live there (without asking for rent).”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3107-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3107-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3107-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3107-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce0c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3108,
      "bookHadithIndex": 227,
      "text": "Abu Salamah bin ‘Abdur-Rahman bin ‘Awf narrated that ‘Abdullah bin ‘Adiy bin Hamra’ said to him:“I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he was on his she-camel, standing in Al-Hazwarah* saying: ‘By Allah, you are the best land of Allah, and the dearest of the land of Allah to me. By Allah, had I not been expelled from you I would never have left.’” *A place in Makkah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3108-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3108-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3108-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3108-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce0d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3109,
      "bookHadithIndex": 228,
      "text": "It was narrated that Safiyyah bint Shaibah said:“I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) delivering a sermon in the Year of the Conquest (of Makkah), and he said: ‘O people, Allah made Makkah sacred the day He created the heavens and the earth, and it is sacred until the Day of Resurrection. Its trees are not to be cut, its game is not to be disturbed, and its lost property is not to be taken except by one who will announce it.’‘Abbas said: ‘Except for Idhkhir (a kind of fragrant grass), for it is (used) for houses and graves.’ The messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘Except for Idhkhir.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3109-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3109-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3109-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce0e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3110,
      "bookHadithIndex": 229,
      "text": "It was narrated from ‘Ayyash bin Abu Rabi’ah (Makhzumi) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:‘The goodness of this nation will not cease as long as they revere this sanctuary* as it is due. But when they lose that reverence, they will be doomed.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3110-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3110-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3110-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3110-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce0f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3111,
      "bookHadithIndex": 230,
      "text": "it was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Faith will retreat to Al-Madinah as a snake retreats to its hole.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3111-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3111-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3111-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3111-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce10",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3112,
      "bookHadithIndex": 231,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:‘Whoever among you can die in Al-Madinah, let him do so, for I will bear witness in favor of those who die there.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3112-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3112-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3112-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3112-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce11",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3113,
      "bookHadithIndex": 232,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“O Allah! Ibrahim was Your Friend and Prophet, and You declared Makkah to be sacred through Ibrahim. O Allah! I am Your slave and Prophet, and I declare what is between its two lava fields to be sacred.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3113-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3113-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3113-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3113-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce12",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3114,
      "bookHadithIndex": 233,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever wishes bad upon the people of Al-Madinah, Allah will cause him to melt as salt melts in water.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3114-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3114-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3114-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3114-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce13",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3115,
      "bookHadithIndex": 234,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Abdullah bin Miknaf said:“I heard Anas bin Malik say: ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Uhud is a mountain which loves us and we love it, and it stands at one of the gates of Paradise. And ‘Aer* stands at one of the gates of Hell.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3115-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3115-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3115-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3115-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce14",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3116,
      "bookHadithIndex": 235,
      "text": "It was narrated that Shaqiq said:“A man sent some Dirham through me to the House.” He said: “I entered the House and Shaibah was sitting on a chair. I handed it (the money) to him and he said: ‘Is this yours?’ I said: ‘No, if it were mine I would not have given it to you.’ He said: ‘Since you say that, ‘Umar was sitting in the place where you are sitting now and said: “I will not go out until I distribute the wealth of the poor Muslims.” I said: “You will not do that.” He said: “I will certainly do that.” He said: “Why is that?” I said: “Because, the Prophet (ﷺ) and Abu Bakr saw where it was, and they had more need of the money than you do. But, they did not move it. Then, he stood up just as he was and went out.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3116-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3116-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3116-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3116-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ce15",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 25,
      "hadithIndex": 3117,
      "bookHadithIndex": 236,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever is in Makkah when the month of Ramadan comes, and he fasts it and prays at night as much as he can, Allah will record for him (reward equivalent to that for) one hundred thousand months of Ramadan observed elsewhere. For each day Allah will record for him (reward equivalent to that for) freeing a slave, and for each day (reward equivalent to that for) providing a horse in the cause of Allah, and for every day merits and for every night merits.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-25-3117-alalbani",
